<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Philip of Montfort</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1205–<a href="/years/1270">1270</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Philip of Montfort was a French crusader baron who became lord of Toron and, from 1246, lord of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tyre">Tyre</a>, where he built up the city's trade. He was a cousin of Simon de Montfort. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baybars">Baybars</a> took Toron in 1266, and in 1270 Philip was murdered in Tyre by an <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/order-of-assassins">Assassin</a> sent at the sultan's instigation.</p></div>
